{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790983773,"nonce":"phfO9JNDScet6VGren1vG51fXjk=","message":"Everything listed is declared and implemented except the theme override. winit's set_theme takes Option\u003cTheme\u003e, where none means follow the system, and x-idl rejects an optional enum argument (\"unsupported argument type in Window.setTheme\"); sent to the x-idl session to add. When it lands, declare\n\n    /// A theme, or none to follow the system's.\n    #[native(window_set_theme)]\n    fn setTheme(this: \u0026Window, theme: Option\u003cEnum\u003cTheme\u003e\u003e);\n\nnatively as w.set_theme(theme.and_then(Theme::from_native).map(native_theme)) over whatever lowering x-idl picks, and as a no-op in a page.\n\nAlso added: setExclusiveFullscreen with Monitor.videoModeCount/videoMode and a VideoMode resource. Run under Ash on 2026-10-03, natively on macOS and in headless Chrome: every operation answered as expected. In the page, inner position and video modes read as their defaults, and setCursorHittest(false) set the canvas's pointer-events to none. Exclusive fullscreen was not run, since it changes the display's mode.","files":null}]}